				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				2002,
				20
			],
			"Message": "style(Wind): Format service implementations and README for consistent line width\n\nApply white-space and formatting normalization across 20 Workbench service implementation files and the project README. All changes are cosmetic — no runtime behavior is modified.\n\n- Insert blank lines before guard clauses in Effect.gen blocks (getBridge checks, etc.) to visually separate the null-check from the bridge operation in WorkbenchActivity, WorkbenchClipboard, WorkbenchCommand, WorkbenchContextKey, WorkbenchDialog, WorkbenchEditor, WorkbenchExtension, WorkbenchHost, WorkbenchKeybinding, WorkbenchLayout, WorkbenchLifecycle, WorkbenchNotification, WorkbenchProduct, WorkbenchProgress, WorkbenchStorage, WorkbenchTheme, and WorkbenchWorkspace\n- Reflow long `__CEL_SERVICES__?.<Name>` property access chains across multiple lines in all 17 bridge-accessor functions\n- Remove unnecessary parentheses around a return object literal in WorkbenchLifecycleLive\n- Rewrap the dynamic import expression in TauriMainProcessService to eliminate a line break after `import(`\n- Add a blank line before the `_eventsListeners` splice call in TelemetryLive\n- Reformat README.md: replace the bare heading with an HTML badge table, wrap long lines consistently at ~90 chars, widen the Component and Service markdown tables to full column width, replace the 4-column markdown sponsor grid with an HTML table containing the Land, PlayForm, NLnet, and NGI0 logos, and re-wrap all paragraph text",
			"SHA": "55e819be8e7ac74af2ce0087ab590aa99f544748"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T00:05:46Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				2002,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Wind): Overhaul README with simplified structure and markdown tables\n\nComplete rewrite of the Wind README to reduce verbosity and modernize formatting. Remove inline HTML tables in favor of plain markdown tables for better readability across platforms. Consolidate the HTML-based logo header, deep-dive component breakdown, and verbose feature list into a concise Overview section with a clean Mermaid architecture diagram.\n\nKey changes: replace the inline HTML `<table>` logo block with a markdown H1 heading and emoji; collapse the four-paragraph introduction into a two-sentence Overview; flatten the Deep Dive section into a flat Architecture list with three bullet points; convert the dark-background project-structure tree into a lighter, comment-free layout; add a dedicated Key Components table with file paths and descriptions; add a \"In the Land Project\" section clarifying Wind's position in the ecosystem; restore the Mermaid graph with updated emoji and simplified labels; replace the four-column HTML partner logo grid with a four-column markdown image table in a compact Funding section; move the Core Architecture Principles table below the project structure for better flow.\n\nNo functional changes — documentation only.",
			"SHA": "f9c47a3d90841848a29cba22cc1887d63a35b39c"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-11T23:28:55Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				2002,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Wind): Add 9 IPC channels for 5 service domains\n\nExtend the IPC channel registry in the Wind service layer with nine new channel constants across five service domains to support additional VS Code workbench and extension host operations.\n\nExtensions (3): `extensions:download`, `extensions:getCoreTranslation`, `extensions:search` — supporting extension lifecycle management beyond install/uninstall. Also alphabetized `extensions:activate` which was previously placed after `extensions:resetPinnedStateForAllUserExtensions`.\n\nOutput (2): `output:dispose`, `output:replace` — enabling output channel lifecycle control.\n\nProcess (1): `process:getMemoryInfo` — exposing memory diagnostics.\n\nSearch (2): `search:cancel`, `search:clearCache` — allowing search lifecycle management.\n\nLanguages (1): `languages:getLanguages` — querying registered language metadata.\n\nThese channels fill gaps in the Wind-to-Mountain IPC surface, enabling feature parity with VS Code's internal channel set.",
			"SHA": "71107a465f71048c4a8769437bd0f0386f668e42"
		},
